In article <1991Jul9.235227.18796@newsserver.sfu.ca> khoo@newsserver.sfu.ca (Alvin Khoo) writes:
>Why could the character not dig thru' the walls of the shops while those
>monster could (drawf, hobbit, etc..) ?
>It took me some time to get the pick-axe into the shops but I could not
>tunnel out.  If I were to tunnel down, the shop keeper would always get
>my pack even when I have dug two rows of pits between us !!!

You can always dig yourself out of a shop, but take care, shops tend to be
on the side of a dungeon, and one cannot dig himself 'from the screen'. You
should try a side towards the middle of the screen. It takes a few tries
to make a hole in the shopwall or floor.  If you don't have any unpaid items
in your inventory nor hase used anything from the shop (i.e. you don't owe
the shopkeeper anything), he won't follow you. The next time you enter the
shop you have already a backdoor, so he is not quick enough to snap you.
Take care that your backdoor is not too close to the shopkeepers door.
